{#
  module/Books/view/books/publications/search-bar.phtml, ported — the literature search
  box, rendered at the top of all three literature pages.

  Expects:
    form              the PublicationsSearchForm from the laminas container
    form_action       /literature/search
    center_on_page    optional; adds the `search-bar-center` class
    advanced_search_url  the advanced-search link, or null when the visitor may not
                      reach it. The .phtml calls `isAllowed('route/publications/advanced-search')`
                      and then assembles the URL; the resource is not in the ACL table at
                      all, so resolving it in the controller is what keeps a
                      never-registered resource from reaching the ACL as a lookup.

  **A GET form**, which is why there is no CSRF token here and no `security` element
  rendered: the search posts nothing and changes nothing. `form_open()` emits
  `method="POST"` unconditionally, so the tag is written out by hand — the one place in
  this batch where the renderer is not used for the opening tag.

  The two assets the .phtml appends through headLink()/headScript() —
  selectize.bootstrap3.css and gen-publications-search-bar.js — are declared by each page
  that includes this, because Twig blocks only work through inheritance and an included
  template cannot contribute to one.

  The `inLanguage` select renders with **translation off**, which the original does by
  toggling `formSelect()->setTranslatorEnabled(false)` around it and back on afterwards:
  the options are language names already localized by the model, and translating them a
  second time turns "Deutsch" into whatever the catalogue has for it.
#}
<div class="row search-bar {% if center_on_page|default(false) %} search-bar-center{% endif %}">
      <div class="col-md-6 col-md-offset-3 col-xs-12">
          <div id="custom-search-input">
            <form method="GET" name="{{ form.getName() }}" action="{{ form_action }}" class="form-horizontal" id="{{ form.getName() }}">
              <div class="input-group col-md-12">
                    {{ form_element(form.get('search')) }}
                  <span class="input-group-btn">
                      <button class="btn btn-info btn-lg" type="submit">
                          <i class="glyphicon glyphicon-search"></i>
                      </button>
                  </span>
              </div>
            <div class="row">
                <div class="col-md-12">
                    <a data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#options" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="options">{{ translate('Advanced options') }}</a>
                    {% if advanced_search_url is not null %}
                        &nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="{{ advanced_search_url }}">{{ translate('Advanced search') }}</a>
                    {% endif %}
                </div>
                <div id="options" class= "collapse row">
                    <div class="checkbox col-md-3">
                        {{ form_element(form.get('showEditionsSeparately')) }}
                    </div>
                    <div class="checkbox col-md-3">
                        {{ form_element(form.get('includeDataSources')) }}
                    </div>
                    <div class="checkbox col-md-3">
                        <div class="pull-right">{{ form_label(form.get('inLanguage')) }}</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="checkbox col-md-3">
                        {{ form_element(form.get('inLanguage'), false) }}
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            </form>
          </div>
      </div>
</div>
